 this was the pre-registered confirmatory test. The rule holds on OLB held-out families: its prediction equals the empirical k* at all 7 reachable margins. It fails on the strongest-quarter split, where it under-predicts by 1–4 grid steps.\n- **Claim in the paper:** the training-side rule is a usable proxy for k*(ε) within the population the model was trained on. That is MTEB held-out groups within one grid step, and OLB held-out families exactly. It is not claimed under a shift in strength or time, where it errs in either direction. MTEB's temporal split over-predicts by 2–6 steps and OLB's strength split under-predicts by 1–4.\n- **Caveat kept:** training and test sides share a population on the held-out-group splits, and this stays in the text.\n\nNo new request is needed. `experiment-repo`#8 (ladder diagnostics for OLB) and `paper-repo`#6 (OLB in the abstract, intro and results, and T1 stated as conditional) are still open."}}, {"id": "e2af999e-1981-5f1a-bb6a-ce7841c90892", "at": 1795738075.1240745, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 59874, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "e9de151e01145a953c4dbbbcce1306c9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "1980710a-2a90-59c7-be87-e433f8c700b7", "at": 1795738075.1274972, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 59875, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "story-repo", "actor": "story-repo", "execution_id": "e9de151e01145a953c4dbbbcce1306c9", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "end_turn", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message → end_turn", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "08bdfca5-a9d0-5ad1-8468-a08d066dfda9", "at": 1795738075.149203, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 59876,